From: Timofey Maykov <itnitro@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] roamd: no self-update check on BE7000 firmware

On MiWRT and Beam WRT roamd is built in the firmware feed for
aarch64_cortex-a73 and updated with the other packages. The upstream feed
has no build for that CPU type, so the check would only ever report an
unreachable index.

Adapted for MiWRT from the Beam WRT patch: also recognise
/etc/miwrt-release.
---
diff --git a/package/roamd/src/mesh_update.c b/package/roamd/src/mesh_update.c
--- a/package/roamd/src/mesh_update.c
+++ b/package/roamd/src/mesh_update.c
@@ -257,6 +257,18 @@ void mesh_self_check(void)
 	if (!job)
 		return;
 
+	/* On BE7000 firmware (MiWRT, Beam WRT) roamd comes from the
+	 * firmware's own signed feed, built for its CPU type, and is updated
+	 * with the other packages. The upstream feed has no build for it, so
+	 * report the installed version as current. */
+	if (!access("/etc/miwrt-release", F_OK) ||
+	    !access("/etc/be7000-release", F_OK)) {
+		selfcheck_write(job, true);
+		free(job);
+
+		return;
+	}
+
 	if (!mesh_self_release(job->branch, sizeof(job->branch), job->arch, sizeof(job->arch))) {
 		selfcheck_write(job, false);
 		free(job);
